# The plan documents. CLAUDE.md states that `plans/` is intentionally
# untracked — the documents are large and have no runtime purpose — but
# nothing enforced it, so thirty of them (001–030) were tracked anyway
# until they were removed in bdb5ea16.
#
# README.md is the exception and stays tracked, because it is the only
# authority on which plan numbers are spent: plan numbers are cited in
# source comments (e.g. "Plan 034" in PassageLine.browser.test.jsx) and
# must never be reused, and `git ls-tree HEAD plans/` cannot tell you
# which are taken now that the documents themselves are ignored.
plans/*.md
!plans/README.md

# Claude Code's project directory. launch.json is real project config --
# it is how the preview tooling knows to start uvicorn on :8000 and vite
# on :5173, and a teammate needs it -- so it is the one exception.
#
# Everything else here is per-machine or disposable: settings.local.json
# is a local override by naming convention, scheduled_tasks.lock is a
# lock, and worktrees/ holds agent worktrees, each a full checkout with
# its own node_modules (17 of them at the time of writing -- large enough
# that `du` on the directory does not finish inside two minutes).
#
# The pattern is `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`: git does not descend
# into an ignored DIRECTORY, so the negation below would never be
# reached. Matching the entries instead keeps launch.json recoverable.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json

# Pre-change dumps from scripts/rescale_intervals.py --apply. They are a
# snapshot of a learner's SRS state, and they are how the migration is
# undone — worth keeping on the machine that ran it, never in the repo.
rescale-restore-*.csv

# ── Repo-wide artifact guards ─────────────────────────────────
#
# backend/.gitignore and frontend/.gitignore already cover their own
# trees thoroughly, and they remain the place to put anything specific
# to one stack. What was missing was the ROOT: a pattern written as
# `.pytest_cache/` inside backend/ only matches under backend/, so
# running pytest from the repo root, or creating a virtualenv beside
# the two package directories, produced artifacts nothing ignored.
# Everything below is written without a leading slash so it matches at
# any depth — defence in depth for the two stack directories, and the
# only cover for the root, docs/ and .github/.
#
# Verified against `git ls-files` when added: no tracked file matches
# any of these patterns, so none of them shadows a file already in the
# repository.

# Python bytecode and tool caches. `__pycache__` appears wherever a
# module is imported from, which includes scripts/ invoked at the root.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Virtualenvs. The backend README installs with a bare `pip install`,
# so the environment is wherever the developer put it — cover the four
# conventional names rather than guess one.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Coverage output. The frontend carries @vitest/coverage-v8 and the
# backend runs pytest; both write here, neither is worth committing.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage/
htmlcov/
*.lcov

# Playwright's run output. CI installs chromium (ci.yml) and the
# vitest browser lane drives it, so a local run leaves both of these.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Node. Only frontend/ has a package.json today, but an `npm install`
# fired from the root creates a second tree that nothing caught.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Logs, at any depth.
*.log

# Conflict and patch leftovers. `git merge` and `git apply --reject`
# write these next to the file they failed on, which is inside the
# source tree — exactly where they are easiest to commit by accident.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*~

# Editor and OS droppings. frontend/.gitignore already has .DS_Store
# for its own tree; these catch the root, backend/ and docs/.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
